course: dictionary
lesson: 14112
title: Rocks that change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Metamorphism is a change in rock. Deep inside the Earth, rock gets very hot and is squeezed by great pressure. It becomes a new kind of rock, but it does not melt.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «Deep under the mountains, the old limestone was baked and squeezed for millions of years.» The rock was heated and squashed, but no one said it melted, so the change happened while it stayed solid. That change is metamorphism.
explain: The new rocks are called metamorphic rocks. Limestone becomes marble, shale becomes slate, and sandstone becomes quartzite. Each one is a changed version of the rock it started as.
fact: Metamorphism is the change of rocks by great heat and pressure deep in the Earth.
fact: Metamorphism changes rock without melting it.
fact: Limestone becomes marble through metamorphism.
fact: Shale becomes slate, and sandstone becomes quartzite.
fact: Metamorphism is one of three ways rocks form, with igneous rocks (from melted rock) and sedimentary rocks (from layers).
exercise: «Deep in the Earth, the rock was baked and squeezed into a new kind of rock, but it never melted.» What is metamorphism? | Melting rock into lava at the surface | Mud settling in layers at the bottom of a lake | *The change of rock by great heat and pressure, without melting it | Rock being worn away by rain and rivers
exercise: Which rock is changed by metamorphism into marble? | Sandstone | Granite | *Limestone | Shale
exercise: Shale changes into which metamorphic rock? | Quartzite | Marble | *Slate | Basalt
test: «Metamorphic rocks are made when rock is heated and squeezed deep down.» Which of these is a metamorphic rock? | Chalk | Pumice | Clay | *Quartzite
test: The rock cycle has three ways rocks form. Which one is NOT one of them? | *Liquid | Metamorphic | Igneous | Sedimentary
exam: «The rock was changed by metamorphism, but it never turned into liquid.» What does this tell you about metamorphism? | *The rock stays solid and becomes a new kind of rock | The rock disappears completely | The rock is made only from loose sand | The rock turns into lava and flows away
